 1 big thing: GTA VI hijacks America 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 An ad for "Grand Theft Auto VI" in Times Square last week. Photo: Michael Nagle/Bloomberg via Getty Images The internet's warring tribes converged yesterday for the loud, lawless debut of " Grand Theft Auto VI ," as 13 years of anticipation culminated in one of the great viral spectacles of all time, Axios' Herb Scribner and Zachary Basu write. 

 💰 By last night, GTA VI had generated an estimated $2.36 billion in sales from nearly 25 million copies — almost triple the first-day revenue of its record-breaking predecessor in 2013, according to Sensor Tower . 

 Millions of players have already downloaded the game to their consoles, with many taking time off work. GTA is "the Star Wars of this generation," Joost van Dreunen, adjunct professor at NYU Stern School of Business, told Reuters . Gameplay clips have already amassed tens of billions of views across X, TikTok, YouTube and other platforms. 🐊 Zoom in: GTA VI drops players into Vice City, a fictionalized Miami that serves as a sprawling digital fever dream of violence, celebrity, corruption and distinctly American absurdity.

 Players can rob banks, steal planes, wrestle alligators and wreak havoc — or pass the afternoon by fishing, shopping, working out and tending to the relationships among the game's characters. A scene from Vice City in "Grand Theft Auto VI." Image : Rockstar Games Zoom out: GTA's return has revived decades-old arguments about whether violent video games encourage real-world aggression, while igniting a far stranger debate over masculinity. 

 The White House posted a minute-long Trump montage, "WELCOME TO MAGA CITY XLVII 🇺🇸🌴," using GTA's font to proclaim "47: The Golden Age." 🎮 " GTA Flu " was coined in 2013 when untold thousands of gamers took days off work to dive headfirst into San Andreas, the game's fictionalized version of Southern California.

 A GameSquare survey found that 30% of employed U.S. gamers were considering taking time off to play. At Fort Stewart, Georgia, 43 soldiers committed to another two to six years of Army service after a four-day GTA gaming pass was included as a reenlistment incentive. The bottom line: GTA offers a glimpse of what monoculture looks like in 2026. For one extraordinary day, the internet had a common story — and a thousand different ways of telling it.

