 4. 🪖 Trump to skeptical Europeans: &quot;Putin wants to end the war&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Maura Kearns/Axios. Photos: Win McNamee/Getty Images, Getty Images Europe via Getty Images.

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 On his way back from China yesterday aboard Air Force One, President Trump phoned in to a meeting his envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner were holding in Berlin with a group of European leaders and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, Axios' Barak Ravid reports. 

 Trump said, according to people in the room: "Putin wants to end the war, he wants the deal done, he is getting tired of this." Why it matters: Instead of turning his historic trilateral summit with Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin into a modern-day Yalta Conference , as some European and Ukrainian officials feared , Trump tried to use it to propel his push for peace in Europe.

 Yes, but: At least one U.S. peace deal reportedly on the table would require Ukraine to surrender territory it still controls in the Donbas region in exchange for NATO membership . 👀 Behind the scenes: When Trump called in to brief the European leaders, he urged them to engage directly with Putin. 

 Trump said, referring to the German host: "Friedrich, you can make a call to Putin and this will make a deal ... Xi respects Zelensky. Putin is ready to do the deal. Zelensky can do a great deal." Read on . 

 
 
