 5. 🤖 Anthropop! 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep . Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Anthropic delivered on the hype: The stock opened at $111.50 — a 34% lift from its $83 offering price — before closing at $97.17.

 The company closed at a market cap of about $1.25 trillion, making it one of the most valuable businesses in the world, Axios' Emily Peck writes. Left: Today's New York Post, California edition. Right: Dario Amodei speaks yesterday at the Nasdaq MarketSite in Manhattan. Photo: Charly Triballeau/AFP via Getty Images 👀 The big picture: There was hope that a big Day 1 pop (an Anthropop, perhaps) would lift the AI trade. It did not.

 The tech-heavy Nasdaq finished the day down 2.25% and is down 9.6% for the past 30 days. Stunning stat: After the first day of trading, Anthropic's 5,300 founders and employees are worth more than the bottom third of U.S. households — 45 million families, according to financial analyst Steve Rattner's calculations . 

