 6. 🗳️ Ossoff wins open-ended &#x27;28 poll 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Graphic : Emerson College Polling (Poll of 1,000 U.S. voters, Nov. 14-16. Margin of error for full poll: ± 3 points.) When Emerson College Polling asked Democratic voters to name their 2028 presidential choice without giving them a list, newly reelected Sen. Jon Ossoff of Georgia drew 17%, Rep. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez got 12%, California Gov. Gavin Newsom got 8% and Kamala Harris got 6%.

 Why it matters: Harris often leads 2028 Democratic polls when the choices are set, reflecting her universal name ID. 🐘 In an open-ended question on the Republican side, 36% of GOP voters named Marco Rubio, 20% JD Vance, 7% Florida Gov. Ron DeSantis, 7% President Trump and 7% maverick Rep. Thomas Massie of Kentucky.

 Between the lines: Rubio has made no move to run. So the result captures the post-midterm angst for Vance. More findings . 

 
 
