 8. 🥧 1 for the road: $35 Thanksgiving 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Lindsey Bailey/Axios. Photo: Library of Congress

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The average cost of a Thanksgiving feast for 10 will be $58.63 this season, up 6% from last year.

 The increase is driven by price hikes for turkey, milk, rolls and cranberries, according to the American Farm Bureau Federation. Zoom in: Walmart is advertising a cheaper Thanksgiving meal than in 2025, Axios' Julianna Bragg reports. 

 The retailer said this year's bundle, which serves 10 people for $35, is its lowest-priced one-click basket ever, down from $39.93 last year. The complete meal comes with a turkey, multiple sides and pumpkin pie to finish.

 It adds ingredients for sweet potato casserole and corn muffins, but drops macaroni and cheese and baby carrots from last year's spread. More meal deals ... Walmart Holiday Trend Report . 

 
 
